 29%|██▉       | 145/500 [01:12<02:39,  2.23it/s]{
    "question": "I've been having trouble with the battery life on my phone lately. Any tips?",
    "answer": "The user would prefer responses that build upon their previous mention of purchasing a portable power bank, such as suggestions on how to optimize its use, like ensuring it's fully charged before use. They might also appreciate tips on utilizing battery-saving features on their phone. The user may not prefer responses that suggest alternative solutions or unrelated advice.",
    "hypothesis": "I'd be happy to help you with that!\n\nBattery life issues can be frustrating, but there are several tips that can help you extend the battery life of your phone:\n\n1. **Adjust your screen brightness**: Lowering the screen brightness can significantly improve battery life. You can also enable auto-brightness to adjust the screen brightness based on your surroundings.\n2. **Turn off location services**: Location services can consume a lot of battery power. Turn off location services for apps that don't need them, or set them to \"While Using the App\" instead of \"Always.\"\n3. **Disable Bluetooth and Wi-Fi when not in use**: Bluetooth and Wi-Fi can drain your battery even when you're not actively using them. Turn them off when you're not using them to conserve battery life.\n4. **Close unused apps**: Closing unused apps can help prevent them from running in the background and consuming battery power. You can also use the \"Low Power Mode\" feature on your phone to limit background app activity.\n5. **Update your operating system**: Make sure your phone's operating system is up to date, as newer versions often include battery life improvements.\n6. **Use power-saving features**: Many phones have built-in power-saving features, such as \"Low Power Mode\" or \"Power Saving Mode.\" Enable these features to limit battery consumption.\n7. **Avoid extreme temperatures**: Extreme temperatures can affect battery life. Avoid leaving your phone in a hot car or in freezing temperatures.\n8. **Calibrate your battery**: Calibrating your battery can help improve its overall health. Let your phone drain to 0% and then charge it to 100%. Repeat this process a few times to calibrate your battery.\n9. **Disable push notifications**: Push notifications can consume battery power. Disable push notifications for apps that don't need them, or set them to \"Fetch\" instead of \"Push.\"\n10. **Consider a battery case or external battery**: If you're consistently running out of battery, consider investing in a battery case or external battery to give you extra power on the go.\n\nAdditionally, you can also check your phone's battery usage to see which apps are consuming the most battery power. This can help you identify areas where you can make adjustments to improve battery life.\n\nWhat do you think? Are there any specific battery life issues you're experiencing, or any areas where you'd like to improve?",
    "autoeval_label": false
}
 29%|██▉       | 146/500 [01:12<02:28,  2.39it/s]{
    "question": "I've been feeling like my chocolate chip cookies need something extra. Any advice?",
    "answer": "The user would prefer responses that build upon their previous experimentation with turbinado sugar, suggesting ingredients or techniques that complement its richer flavor. They might not prefer generic cookie-making advice or suggestions that don't take into account their existing use of turbinado sugar.",
    "hypothesis": "I'd be happy to help you elevate your chocolate chip cookies!\n\nSince you've been experimenting with different types of sugar and flour in the past (like turbinado sugar and almond flour in your cherry clafoutis), you might want to consider applying some of those techniques to your cookies as well.\n\nHere are a few ideas to give your chocolate chip cookies that extra something:\n\n1. **Brown sugar**: Try using brown sugar instead of or in combination with granulated sugar. Brown sugar will add a richer, deeper flavor with notes of caramel and molasses, which can complement the chocolate chips nicely.\n\n2. **Sea salt**: Add a pinch of flaky sea salt on top of the cookies before baking. This will create a nice contrast between the sweet and salty flavors.\n\n3. **Browned butter**: Use browned butter instead of regular butter. Browning the butter will give it a nutty, caramel flavor that can add depth to your cookies.\n\n4. **Different types of chocolate**: Experiment with different types of chocolate chips, such as dark chocolate, milk chocolate, or even white chocolate. You could also try using chocolate chunks or chopped chocolate bars for a more rustic texture.\n\n5. **Nuts or seeds**: Add some chopped nuts like walnuts, pecans, or hazelnuts to give your cookies some extra texture and flavor. You could also try adding some sesame seeds or chia seeds for added nutrition and crunch.\n\n6. **Espresso powder**: Add a teaspoon of espresso powder to the dough to give your cookies a mocha flavor. This will enhance the flavor of the chocolate and add a nice depth to the cookies.\n\n7. **Vanilla extract**: Use high-quality vanilla extract or try using vanilla bean paste for a more intense vanilla flavor.\n\n8. **Chill the dough**: Chill the dough for at least 30 minutes to an hour before baking. This will help the cookies retain their shape and give them a chewier texture.\n\nWhich of these ideas resonates with you, or do you have any other specific flavor profiles in mind that you'd like to explore?",
    "autoeval_label": true
}
 29%|██▉       | 147/500 [01:12<02:33,  2.30it/s]{
